&lt;/span&gt; Technical Writeup PDF&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</content:encoded></item><item><title>Safety Valve (Öryggisventill)</title><link>https://jamesrobb.ca/projects/safety_valve/</link><pubDate>Thu, 09 Apr 2015 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><author>me@jamesrobb.ca (James Robb)</author><guid>https://jamesrobb.ca/projects/safety_valve/</guid><description/><content:encoded>&lt;p&gt;In collaboration with others in the Pirate Party of Iceland, I created Safety Valve. Safety Valve is a platform that allows the residents of Iceland to act as a shadow parliament of sorts. Each bill currently moving through Icelandic parliament is converted into a petition. Residents can then digitally sign for or against each petition using their Ice Key, a digital authentication mechanism provided by the Icelandic government. We ran it for a couple years but it is unfortunately no longer online.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;All of the code is hosted on &lt;a href="https://github.com/piratar/safetyvalve"&gt;Github &lt;span class="iconwrapper"&gt;
